<title>BELGIUM: D'IETEREN 1996 PROFIT TRIPLES.</title>
<headline>D'IETEREN 1996 PROFIT TRIPLES.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-02-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year to Dec 31, 1996</p>
<p>(in million of Belgian francs unless stated)</p>
<p>    Group net profit			    1,622 vs     534</p>
<p>    Cons net current			    2,316 vs   1,102</p>
<p>    Gross dividend (francs)			50 vs	44</p>
<p>NOTE - D'Ieteren is Belgium's largest car importer and</p>
<p>distributor. It imports and distributes Volkswagen group (VW,</p>
<p>Audi, Seat and Skoda) and Porsche vehicles.</p>
<p>The company has 77.1 percent of car rental firm Avis Europe,</p>
<p>which is due to be partly listed on the London Stock Exchange.</p>
<p>    Depreciation for goodwill		   694 vs     568</p>
<p>Cons turnover from car imports and</p>
<p>    distribution activities		  53,129 vs  47,253</p>
<p>-- Bert Lauwers, Brussels Newsroom +32 2 287 6815, Fax +32 2</p>
<p>230 7710</p>
